class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindred of the East count as VtM by the way? Or seperate line? </div> </div> </div>I actually prefer KotE's approach because (ignoring the ones who got pulled into Yomi because the Yama Kings are greedy) they were actually people who earned damnation in life and have a second chance, which they can take or take advantage of. The &quot;clawing you way out of hell back into your corpse and roving as a gibbering undead horror until somebody tortures some sense into you&quot; is also fun. But I specifically meant the Cainites here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyhow, I think you are a little bit... harsh with Vampire<br /> The end of Beckett's Jyhad Diary summaries it nicely </div> </div> </div>I do remember that bit; this -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>You who read this need to know that the Jyhad \u2014 our eternal struggle \u2014 is what you make of it.<br /> You can be a beast, you can be an angel with fangs, and you can be so much more besides.<br /> Fear not the strings of puppet masters. Dwell not upon who controls your fate.<br /> We must all face tomorrow. Do so with open eyes and an open heart, and embrace our future.<br /> Never falter. Do not break. There is always another sunset.</i> </div> </div> </div>- is how I approach vampire. But it doesn't feel like it's how the authors (or many of the fans) approach it nine times out of ten.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T08:17:13-07:00","id":1514956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514946#post1514946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is maddening, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea...<br /> Actually, you do, but you know hat I ment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514946#post1514946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually prefer KotE's approach</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Yeah, you are right<br /> Actually the Followers of Set should be like the Kuei-jin, but instead of the Thousand Hell of Yomi a potential Settie should be an escapee from Duat - the egyptian underworld basically Hell if you are not in a tiny portion of it aka. manage to gain acces to the Field of Reeds, where Osiris rules<br /> Serpents, the spawn of Apep, haunt the 12 caverns of Duat. They swim in the river and coil about the limbs of the unredeemed dead.<br /> The dead in Duat exist in darkness, blinded by it, relieved only by the nightly passage of the ship of Ra<br /> Along with their torments, the dead in Duat cannot breathe or speak. The &quot;Opening of the Mouth&quot; funerary ritual was meant to deliver the deceased from this unhappy condition.<br /> The dead in Duat rest in coffins, paralized, that open only when the sun-god Ra makes his nightly passage.<br /> Just to name a few<br /> Duat is... not the nicest place, it is literally Hell if you don't cheat your way thrugh it, filled with darkness, silence, sand, snakes, demons and quite nasty things even the Sun God have to fight and Mandjet, the <i>Boat</i> of <i>Millions of Years</i>\u200b needs quite a fighter crew to help him out (and the mightiest of them was <b>Sutekh...</b>)... even the domain of <b>Seker</b>, the original God of the Underworld whom Osiris basically dethroned, Imhet was seen as difficult, sandy terrain, not to mention according to the myth, Seker rules the Fifth Kingdom of Night, which is called &quot;Hidden&quot;, and is tasked with punishing the souls of evildoers by throwing them into a boiling lake. Only a tiny part is &quot;good&quot;, the Field of Reeds and the personal domain of Osiris... and there is the whole Scales and Feather of Ma'at against your heart, the 42 Judges who destroy you if you don't know their name, <b>Ammit</b> eagerly awaits to eat your soul if you fail the Scales<br /> And thats for the &quot;normal dead&quot;!<br /> However, when the damned died? Their flesh was torn away by demons and their mummy wrappings were removed so that their bodies were left to decompose. In the underworld that the blessed successfully navigate, their order of things is reversed, even to the extent that the damned have to walk upside down, eat their own excrement and drink their own urine. Their hands are tied behind their backs, often around stakes. Their heads and limbs are severed from their bodies and their flesh is cut off their bones. Their hearts are removed and their ba-souls are separated from their bodies, forever unable to return to them. They even loose their shadows, which were considered an important part of the ancient Egyptian being. They have no air and suffer from hunger and thirst, as they receive no funerary offerings. Worst of all, they are denied the reviving light of the sun god, who ignores them, even as they cry out load and wail when he passes them in the underworld at night.<br /> They are continuously punished by demons, who are the representatives of chaos. Indeed, the demons are often recruited from the ranks of the damned themselves, so that they torture and kill one another. They are subjected to knives and swords and to the fire of hell, often kindled by fire spitting snakes. These horrible punishments were carried out in the &quot;slaughtering place&quot; or &quot;place of destruction&quot;, and presided over by the fierce goddess <b>Sekhmet</b>, whose butchers hack their victims to pieces and burn them with inextinguishable fire, sometimes in deep pits or in cauldrons in which they are scorched, cooked and reduced to ashes. Demons feed on their entrails and drink their blood.<br /> Another location was the Lake of Fire, which was first mentioned in the Book of Two Ways in the Coffin Text (Spell 1054/1166) and illustrated in the Book of the Dead (Chapter 126). Like the &quot;outer darkness,&quot; it is a place of regeneration for the sun god and his blessed followers, to whom it provides nourishment and cool water, but a place of destruction for the damned. Birds even fly away from it when they experience the burning, bloody water and small the stench of putrefaction which rises from it. In chapter 126 of the Book of the Dead, its shores are guarded by four baboons who sit at the bow of the barque of Ra and who are usually connected to the sunrise. There, they act as judges of the divine tribunal in order to decide who might be granted access through &quot;the secret portals of the West&quot; and who will be delivered to the hellhound, who, according to another spell, is in charge of this place. That demon-god is the &quot;Swallower of Millions,&quot; responsible for devouring corpses, or their shadows, snatching hearts and inflicting injury without being seen (<b>Am-heh</b> was a dangerous god from the underworld whose name can be translated as 'devourer of millions', or eater of eternity. He lived in a lake of fire and was represented as a man with the head of a hunting dog.)<br /> Not to mention <b>Shezmu</b>\u200b, Demon-God of the Wine Press, Oils and Slaughterer of the Damned; after the deceased had died, it was he who caught the sinful ones for punishment. In Chapter 175 of The Book of the Dead Shesmu was known as &quot;Lord of the Blood&quot;. It was under the orders of Osiris, that he would chop up the evil ones, take their heads and toss them into a wine press, treating the heads as if they were grapes to create blood wine.<br /> \u200b<br /> The judgement of Ma'at and devoured by Ammit was actually an &quot;easy death&quot; compared others\u200b<br /> <br /> In this regard Sutekh came back from Hell, like the souls come back/escape from Yomi. Apophis (and even other gods of Duat) like the Yama Kings<br /> The Followers of Set calls themselves the Mesu Bedshet, the &quot;<i>Children</i> of <i>Rebellion</i>&quot; for a reason - with a twist, this makes the Children of Anubis, the Silent Striders technically the jailors of Duat/Hell the &quot;bad guys&quot; and enemies of the Followers of Set, just they forgot the reason\u200b<br /> <br /> Would make much more sense, considering the whole belief system of the Followers of Sutekh to be like the Kuei-jin rather like the get of Caine<br /> Or actually sell Sutekh as Caine... the murdering of thy brother is a tiny bit older story with Sutekh and Asar/Set and Osiris than Caine and Able...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T08:40:08-07:00","id":1514958,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I can pick a definitive choice about whose condition is worse between Wraiths and Vampires, from an IC perspective. While the suffering of a Wraith *can* be fleeting, it's worth remembering that plenty of them are centuries old, if not millennia. And the suffering of a Vampire can end any time the Vampire wants if annihilation is considered an acceptable outcome.<br /> <br /> I think that Vampire tends to lean harder on the idea that their condition is a curse because that's pretty much the only thing keeping it from being *just* Comic Book Heroes and Villains With Fangs. To be clear, I'm not trying to bash that playstyle. But the writers were definitely leaning more towards Anne Rice than <i>Near Dark</i> with their original concept for the game, so making being a Vampire suck unless you *really* want to lean into it makes sense from that perspective.<br /> <br /> Like, from the outside you can look at a Vampire and talk about their &quot;pitiable&quot; condition, and that wouldn't be wrong in many respects. But from the perspective of a Vampire that's decided to go all-in, it's probably a God Damn Blast. Whether they rapidly descend into Wightdom or manage to adopt a Path of Enlightenment, a Vampire that abandons Humanity and embraces their new condition may not feel very cursed at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:30:28-07:00","id":1514970,"title":"","content":"Kharnov is right: vampires are set up to have a blast. It's a high cost, high reward kind of lifestyle. <br /> <br /> Pros:<br /> feeding is the most euphoric thing ever. It's not subjective, it's just the best (bar any spell specifically designed to cause pleasure, but those are pretty dangerous) <br /> You'll improve rather than atrophy as you age. You might not be great now, but you sure will be amazing years from now.<br /> If you play your cards right, immortality. you might even live long enough to see the release of half-life 3. <br /> actually knowing what's going on in the world<br /> You'll be able to create a cadre of people who love and worship you without much difficulty or even emotional investment. <br /> You will never need a normal job to make ends meet. <br /> The &quot;I control animals&quot; power<br /> The &quot;do as I say&quot; power<br /> The &quot;I'm not here&quot; power<br /> The &quot;I can jump six meters and swat you away like a beach ball&quot; power.<br /> The &quot;literally magic&quot; powers. <br /> The &quot;Bullet resistant&quot; power<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> You can only be up at night, that's most of every day gone! Being up when nobody else is can be quite a drag. <br /> You need to lie to people on a daily basis and keep a secret. <br /> Politics is shit, but it was when you were mortal, you're just closer to it now. <br /> If you don't get your fix or surround yourself with problems, you might lose control and drain folks or worse, cause a scene. <br /> If you're way too evil, you get uglier and lose control more. <br /> <br /> All this damnation talk is just Toreador posturing/writers trying to keep player characters relatable and preventing players from building crazy (reverse) harems and living like hedonistic gods. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:25:18-07:00","id":1514980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514958#post1514958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I can pick a definitive choice about whose condition is worse between Wraiths and Vampires, from an IC perspective. While the suffering of a Wraith *can* be fleeting, it's worth remembering that plenty of them are centuries old, if not millennia. And the suffering of a Vampire can end any time the Vampire wants if annihilation is considered an acceptable outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>They overlap a lot in experience (being cut off from one's life, political corruption, slavery, parasitic behaviours regarding the living that can involve some really fucked up things to get your fix, Psyche-vs-Shadow/Man-vs-Beast, dangers of being consumed by something really ugly...). In some ways Wraiths are the worse off, because at least vampires get some of the benefits on being on the other side of the Shroud and since Vicissitude isn't in-clan for everybody they have less of a human-furniture problem. Where vampire depresses me just a tiny bit more is that giving into Oblivion is the bad end for a Wraith, but it feels like if a vampire wants to jump in that's, in-universe, preferable to them continuing to struggle and exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, from the outside you can look at a Vampire and talk about their &quot;pitiable&quot; condition, and that wouldn't be wrong in many respects. But from the perspective of a Vampire that's decided to go all-in, it's probably a God Damn Blast. Whether they rapidly descend into Wightdom or manage to adopt a Path of Enlightenment, a Vampire that abandons Humanity and embraces their new condition may not feel very cursed at all. </div> </div> </div>True, and frankly, they've probably got it right as far as canon goes. It doesn't change the fact that there's something so fundamentally wrong with the universe that the attitude seems to be that you could have a shovelhead party after finding a troupe of girl scouts on a camping trip, and then those murdered prepubescent girls are now all stuck with the choice of terminal sunbathing or being forsaken in the eyes of god, to be cleansed off the face of the Earth come Gehenna and this is how things should be.<br /> (Also, apparently, that was playing vampire incorrectly or something? :P)\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514970#post1514970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this damnation talk is just Toreador posturing/writers trying to keep player characters relatable and preventing players from building crazy (reverse) harems and living like hedonistic gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to agree, but I feel like the writers intended the woe and damnation and End of Days thing to be quite literal, rather than melodramatic Toreador tripe. After all, V5 had to be created to really hammer home <i>How This Game Is Supposed To Be Played</i>.<br /> <br /> Different note regarding the list of cons; I tend to expand their active hours to start at civil twilight. It might not give that much time, but if we stick to the true night hours we're never going to have time for anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-14-2023, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:40:28-07:00","id":1514983,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's the result of me jumping on late and not really being exposed to Y2K but THE END IS NIGH has always and probably will always be a part of the human psych and it's quite easy to dismiss. Maybe as Vampires are supernatural beings and have some proof of higher existences they've got more reason to fear things but it's also written that a few Antideluvians were openly active in the 15th century and never felt the need to become apocalyptic monsters. I think it makes a lot of sense that some elders are worried that their grandsires will exit their long torpors and usurp everything they've built but I'd hardly call that the end of days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:04:55-07:00","id":1514993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514980#post1514980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, and frankly, they've probably got it right as far as canon goes. It doesn't change the fact that there's something so fundamentally wrong with the universe that the attitude seems to be that you could have a shovelhead party after finding a troupe of girl scouts on a camping trip, and then those murdered prepubescent girls are now all stuck with the choice of terminal sunbathing or being forsaken in the eyes of god, to be cleansed off the face of the Earth come Gehenna and this is how things should be.<br /> (Also, apparently, that was playing vampire incorrectly or something? :P)\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>How things ARE and how things SHOULD BE are veeerrry different things. The one constant across World of Darkness game-lines is that the entire cosmos is basically circling the drain, so the status quo should probably not be viewed as functional or just. Or if it is, it's part of one of those annoying mind-screw apologetics arguments where somehow the best possible world is going to emerge from a whirlwind of radioactive feces.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:05:09-07:00","id":1514994,"title":"","content":"Vampire should be a power fantasy that only stops being appealing the moment you stop to think all the sex, drugs, blood, power and wealth comes at the mere price of your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:45:42-07:00","id":1515021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514994#post1514994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire should be a power fantasy that only stops being appealing the moment you stop to think all the sex, drugs, blood, power and wealth comes at the mere price of your soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, according to some religions and their interpretations drawing an animal, getting an earring, or having the wrong lineage/genes is enough to damn your soul. I can only roll my eyes at your statement. Give me soul-loss mechanics or give me death. Actually, willpower is the closest thing we've got to a soul I think. Maybe botching a thaumaturgy roll will better damn you than murderous arson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T15:02:07-07:00","id":1515023,"title":"","content":"The DA Roads and their Paths are actually pretty good at encapsulating the most common motivations a vampire might tackle their unlives with (and on a meta level the modes in which you can play the game), imo. You want angst, go Heaven. You want to party, go Sin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T15:44:48-07:00","id":1515027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514994#post1514994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire should be a power fantasy that only stops being appealing the moment you stop to think all the sex, drugs, blood, power and wealth comes at the mere price of your soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, vampires' souls is hardly any different than human ones. They have the same chance of becoming wraith after all.<br /> <br /> The only difference is the presence of a sleeping avatar in living human, but let's be honest, most humans won't touch awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T16:37:24-07:00","id":1515035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515021#post1515021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, according to some religions and their interpretations drawing an animal, getting an earring, or having the wrong lineage/genes is enough to damn your soul. I can only roll my eyes at your statement. Give me soul-loss mechanics or give me death. Actually, willpower is the closest thing we've got to a soul I think. Maybe botching a thaumaturgy roll will better damn you than murderous arson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, you have indeed described my point. If you don't care about being a monster, being a vampire is awesome.<br /> <br /> If you do, it's a horrifying curse that comes with cool powers.<br /> <br /> Basically, V:TM is a magical version of Grand Theft Auto. You are completely devoid of society's checks on your behavior except for a handful of rules that will get you killed. You may be murdered by the Prince or Anarchs eventually but it is a helluva ride. Murder, mayhem, and rampages are all possible as long as you don't leave a whiff of the Masquerade being broken or destroy someone's pet human or favorite museum.<br /> <br /> However, while you CAN play Claude, you can also play Nico Bellic. Who doesn't WANT to be a hitman but really can't be anything else.\u200b<br /> <br /> And while you may LOVE being a monster like Claude, well, it doesn't change the fact that atheist or Buddhist or not, you're a piece of shit people should hold in contempt.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, vampire with no conscience, you're Jeffrey Epstein. You may not know it but you're still a monster to everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-14-2023, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T19:46:52-07:00","id":1515052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline#post1514933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, what I get from VtM</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the key thing that determines what a game line is or isn't. The personal thing you connect to makes or breaks the meaning of the game setting and system.<br /> <br /> If you are the sort of person who needs to be seen as good, needs validation of others or society at large, needs to right the wrongs of an imperfect system.... then yeah, vampire is the stuff of nightmares. Your existence is a blight upon the world, you can never be truly known because you must hide, and you have all eternity to contemplate how much everything sucks.<br /> <br /> If you are the sort of person who yearns for tragedy and loss, the feeling being innately doomed and cursed, the knowledge that everything good is transitory at best, but suffering is eternal, then VtM is your pity party drug of choice.<br /> <br /> If you are the kind of person that is more the adapt and overcome type, where violence and cruelty is neither embraced nor avoided, then VtM is just a continuation of your story. You feed on others yes, but you don't have to kill to eat. You have to fight to survive, but so does every other living thing on the planet. Yes you can be alone in the dark, but that doesn't mean you have to be uncomfortable with it.<br /> <br /> The reality is that the first two types of vampires, which seem to make up most of the trope PC character types would not survive as vampires for very long. The third type however would survive and indeed potentially thrive as a vampire. The annoying thing is that vampire society seems designed to cater to the first two types, rather than the third which would be the only ones around. But that is an entirely different discussion.<br /> <br /> I have run vampire games that were incredibly silly (vampire idol band on tour) and I have run vampire games that messed with people's heads (play as self, accidentally butcher family members). The game is only a canvas for the ST and players to project their own psyches onto the table. If you are comfortable with being dangerous or monstrous, then there is little &quot;personal horror&quot; to be had in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T19:48:18-07:00","id":1515053,"title":"","content":"A concept I created for a character (for a fanfic in this case) was a Malkavian with multiple personalities, or a Tzimice with fluid gender, I haven't decided, that he takes care of a hospital and the place is quite well equipped. and tidy, an example of professionalism, but he would have there underground where there would be several prisoners that he would have taken over the years, just the garbage of society that no one will miss, not indigents, but people who at least have already committed homicide or abuse , they stay there supplying blood and when they get too old or no longer serve they become donors, would he call that &quot;cleansing&quot;, so would he be a hateful Kindred? By the way that was rhetorical, of course it would be hateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T20:27:36-07:00","id":1515054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515052#post1515052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is the key thing that determines what a game line is or isn't. The personal thing you connect to makes or breaks the meaning of the game setting and system.<br /> <br /> If you are the sort of person who needs to be seen as good, needs validation of others or society at large, needs to right the wrongs of an imperfect system.... then yeah, vampire is the stuff of nightmares. Your existence is a blight upon the world, you can never be truly known because you must hide, and you have all eternity to contemplate how much everything sucks.<br /> <br /> If you are the sort of person who yearns for tragedy and loss, the feeling being innately doomed and cursed, the knowledge that everything good is transitory at best, but suffering is eternal, then VtM is your pity party drug of choice.<br /> <br /> If you are the kind of person that is more the adapt and overcome type, where violence and cruelty is neither embraced nor avoided, then VtM is just a continuation of your story. You feed on others yes, but you don't have to kill to eat. You have to fight to survive, but so does every other living thing on the planet. Yes you can be alone in the dark, but that doesn't mean you have to be uncomfortable with it.<br /> <br /> The reality is that the first two types of vampires, which seem to make up most of the trope PC character types would not survive as vampires for very long. The third type however would survive and indeed potentially thrive as a vampire. The annoying thing is that vampire society seems designed to cater to the first two types, rather than the third which would be the only ones around. But that is an entirely different discussion.<br /> <br /> I have run vampire games that were incredibly silly (vampire idol band on tour) and I have run vampire games that messed with people's heads (play as self, accidentally butcher family members). The game is only a canvas for the ST and players to project their own psyches onto the table. If you are comfortable with being dangerous or monstrous, then there is little &quot;personal horror&quot; to be had in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's actually how the world is structured. V:TM is a game with an exspiration date. You will either become a monster or you will die a hero. The price of survival long-term in V:TM is you lose gradually everything cool or redeemable about yourself. It's why Neonates can team up with each other but only a handful of Elders will. Eventually, all Coteries break up due to the betrayals and corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T21:23:28-07:00","id":1515058,"title":"","content":"I think that Vampire: the Masquerade session and chronicles can have protagonists, villains, antagonists, characters, and heroes who are - despite dark or sadistic inclinations, potentially troublesome requirements, and specific obsessions - positive, confident, brave, unique, wise, and ambitious. <br /> <br /> In V:tM books ( and also in M:tA supplements, and as well the rest of wider WoD ) there are many good, interesting, and curious descriptions of characters who cleartly and certainly stand up for or represent concepts, ideas, passions, and ideologies.<br /> <br /> The various groups of Vampires - and other vampiric, undead, and darkness-related - like Revenants, for example Obertus Revenants or Zantosa Revenants - are contstructed and maintained with precision, zeal, perfection, and dedication. This includes Vampire Clans, Vampiric Sects, Kindred Bloodlines, and Revenant Families. These establishments and groups can certainly help in clear, interesting, positive, definitive, and optimistic advanament and progression through the Modern Nights - with all the glory, beauty, purpose, and meaning that a Vampiress ( or a Ghoul, or a Revenant ) would for herself consider and desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T22:16:42-07:00","id":1515060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515058#post1515058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The various groups of Vampires - and other vampiric, undead, and darkness-related - like Revenants, for example Obertus Revenants or Zantosa Revenants - are contstructed and maintained with precision, zeal, perfection, and dedication. This includes Vampire Clans, Vampiric Sects, Kindred Bloodlines, and Revenant Families. These establishments and groups can certainly help in clear, interesting, positive, definitive, and optimistic advanament and progression through the Modern Nights - with all the glory, beauty, purpose, and meaning that a Vampiress ( or a Ghoul, or a Revenant ) would for herself consider and desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you able to work this out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:06:01-07:00","id":1515063,"title":"","content":"I have noticed that many players confuse &quot;horror&quot; with &quot;depressing&quot;. But that is not the case. Some horror, of course, can be nihilistic and lend itself to depressing. But horror, and especially gothic horror, is part of the romantic tradition. And the romantic can incorporate many things that elevate it from anything depressing. I admit that this is something that the Revised era often forgot as it reacted against certain notions that the earlier editions lend itself not to &quot;horror&quot; but the &quot;super-hero&quot; genre (the &quot;Vampions&quot; concept).<br /> <br /> Another mistake is for some players to confuse tragedy with &quot;depressing&quot;. I am firmly in the camp that vampires are monsters that should always be destroyed. But that does not mean that vampire characters that struggle with morality are nihilistic or depressing figures. They are instead <i>tragic</i> figures. And there can be many positive emotions that come from that tragedy.<br /> <br /> I think the actual issue is that some players play up nihilistic themes with vampire, confusing that with the concept of horror. Or simply want their power fantasies associated with vampirism to be affirmed, that they are shocked to hear other players bring up the negative aspects of vampirism.<br /> <br /> Horror is to frighten. But that is not the same as to depress. The two can coincide, but I think in good games there should be enough other things to prevent the chronicle into descending into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:34:26-07:00","id":1515068,"title":"","content":"I think for me it's important to emphasize that the horror of VTM is less about the vampire's feelings or connection to god and more about the impact they have on the people around them. <br /> <br /> Your ghoul gets a divorce and loses custody because he spends all his nights with you, and he's happy about that, at least till the blood bond wears off. <br /> You siphon away resources people need so you can waste them in petty squabbles and dick measuring contests. <br /> Your indulgences have the occasional accident that get someone innocent killed but you've got the power to get away with this with some freequency and you'll almost certainly do it again if you live longer. <br /> You vigorously fight any anti-corruption attempts from mortal govermnets and do your best to interfere with the democratic processes all so you can have more money and a better time feeding. <br /> Your best friends are also slimeballs you'll support at the expense of the masses. <br /> If you're killed, the system will replace you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T01:08:28-07:00","id":1515071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515063#post1515063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed that many players confuse &quot;horror&quot; with &quot;depressing&quot;. But that is not the case. Some horror, of course, can be nihilistic and lend itself to depressing. But horror, and especially gothic horror, is part of the romantic tradition. And the romantic can incorporate many things that elevate it from anything depressing. I</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a case of personal mileage and preference rather than confusion, because the romantic beats often do nothing to elevate the horror elements out of depressing for me. The books hammer in the nihilism so hard (as sometimes do discussions) leaves me exhausted and apathetic to the matter, or angry at best; so, it's depressing for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another mistake is for some players to confuse tragedy with &quot;depressing&quot;. I am firmly in the camp that vampires are monsters that should always be destroyed. But that does not mean that vampire characters that struggle with morality are nihilistic or depressing figures. They are instead <i>tragic</i> figures. And there can be many positive emotions that come from that tragedy. </div> </div> </div>If they deserve destruction no matter what, end of story, then they are tragic <i>and</i> depressing and no positive emotions could hold any meaning and I stop caring. As I said, this is down to personal mileage.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not that I don't appreciate the nihilistic horror, vampire just pushes a little hard. And I don't think I'm responding well to the Religious Horror elements. My games are still nihilistic and the characters tragic, but they're either toned down a tad and not inherently damned/doomed, or else we're going on a Religious Horror Gnostic-themed journey where the Setites were right all along and the pack/coterie's off to punch the Demiurge in the face for doing this to them... The latter of which is probably veering into vampions territory I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-15-2023, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T01:51:17-07:00","id":1515074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515068#post1515068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for me it's important to emphasize that the horror of VTM is less about the vampire's feelings or connection to god and more about the impact they have on the people around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make it one part that and one part the effect other vampires have on<i> you </i>(99% of the population is unsafe to trust, and finding that 1% is a massive leap of faith that can fuck you over; Everything you dare to love is a target for your enemies. Hide most of yourself (your thoughts, said loves, dreams...), lest you lose them; Always double-guess everything nice anyone ever does for you; Never, ever be vulnerable, etc) Enjoy your paranoia, repressed emotions, strained relationships and loneliness while you're trapped in the politically toxic criminal empire that leads you to blight the lives of those around you.<br /> <br /> And while we're at it, enjoy the realisation that the only reason you're worse than the kine is because they lack the means and societal pressure and would be just as bad as you in your shoes (if not worse). A few centuries of built up misanthropy and disgust at the historical attrocities they've lived through (many caused by mortals on their own) is the leading cause of Elders seemingly being uncaring bastards; they're tired, the world doesn't deserve the effort and it's easier to focus on the few, secret things they care about and the positives of power.<br /> <br /> (And then I soften it with the fact that actually, being a vampire can be great fun and doesn't have to be misery 24/7. The True-Love merit exists (and I'm using the variants where it doesn't have to be a mortal, shut up V20). You can go on Trenchcoats and Katanas style missions, sometimes with a bit of unironic vampion behaviour as a treat. Backstabbing vampire politics is more often a game to played than anything serious. Super-speed rooftop parkour races are fun. Hell I'd even borrow from Twilight's baseball scene; vampire sports in secure hidden locations where you can stop holding back and just play with your powers...)<br /> <br /> God is a special tool we only bring out for very specific games that lean on the Punk half of VtM's genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-15-2023, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:52:30-07:00","id":1515079,"title":"","content":"Other vampires are a pain but the majority being unsafe to trust is something you'd only see in very dysfunctional cities. At the very least, your sire is investing in you and wants to see that investment pay off. You should never assume vampires will do the morally right thing but you can assume they'll do the politically right thing, and that's a reasonable basis for a measured amount of trust. As much as proletarian writers want to make vampires a mockery of bourgeoise villainy, it's really not in their best interests to bully competent or at least promising neonates that aren't directly challenging them. You are all in the conspiracy together after all. Petty tricks will be seen through eventually. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think the next VTM game should have a &quot;mindset&quot; coach instructing players how to fit into the vampire political system. The game says something like &quot;your new character probably just came out of their sire's tutelage&quot;. But most pcs are directed with their player's anti-capitalist angst, despite being the bourgeoise of the story. Your sire really should've filled you up with a more harmonious attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:12:59-07:00","id":1515084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515079#post1515079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the next VTM game should have a &quot;mindset&quot; coach instructing players how to fit into the vampire political system. The game says something like &quot;your new character probably just came out of their sire's tutelage&quot;. But most pcs are directed with their player's anti-capitalist angst, despite being the bourgeoise of the story. Your sire really should've filled you up with a more harmonious attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... very unlikely to happen in. If it did, it wouldn't be the way you think vampires should function. We're having a clash of how individual players think the game should work and how the writers think it should work (for example, Justin Achilli, who I believe was responsible for a mechanic in Requiem 1e where vampires were instinctively hostile to each other<i> on sight </i>(2e dropped it)). The &quot;Eternal Struggle&quot; is all about how everybody is lying and using each other as pawns in bigger player's games and blah blah blah. You can change it, but that is how canon VtM works. Like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> endless games of brinksmanship in which vampires contest one another\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this primitive urge to hoard all available blood all for<br /> oneself finds outlet in conspiracy and gamesmanship.<br /> What one Kindred wants, another hoards, another has<br /> plans to steal, and still another can distract them all<br /> and seize a momentary advantage.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cA prince never lacks legitimate<br /> reasons to break his promise,\u201d\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such perspectives are the bylaws of the Kindred\u2019s<br /> eternal war against one another, and with centuries or<br /> millennia behind the individual feuds in the Jyhad, it<br /> is no wonder that the Damned play their cards so close<br /> to their chest.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The image it's painting from where I'm standing is one where we're expected to believe while they won't be stupid enough to jeopardise their existence, vampires are all scheming against each other 24/7* and can never trust each other. (*...or however many hours of night-time activity we have/7)<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and bullying neonates and fledglings was one of the examples given for the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the brash young Brujah really hate the<br /> Toreador ancilla who snubbed her at a party? Or did<br /> the Ventrue elder encourage his great-grandchilde to<br /> hustle the inexperienced Brujah sire into introducing<br /> his progeny too soon into Kindred society in the hopes<br /> that the Toreador would make a move?\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-15-2023, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:10:22-07:00","id":1515093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515068#post1515068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for me it's important to emphasize that the horror of VTM is less about the vampire's feelings or connection to god and more about the impact they have on the people around them.<br /> <br /> Your ghoul gets a divorce and loses custody because he spends all his nights with you, and he's happy about that, at least till the blood bond wears off.<br /> You siphon away resources people need so you can waste them in petty squabbles and dick measuring contests.<br /> Your indulgences have the occasional accident that get someone innocent killed but you've got the power to get away with this with some freequency and you'll almost certainly do it again if you live longer.<br /> You vigorously fight any anti-corruption attempts from mortal govermnets and do your best to interfere with the democratic processes all so you can have more money and a better time feeding.<br /> Your best friends are also slimeballs you'll support at the expense of the masses.<br /> If you're killed, the system will replace you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This take confuses me. None of what you listed is horror, at best it is just how the world works and at worst it's just banality.<br /> <br /> A General can order his conscripted troops to fight and die with no consideration for the families the troops leave behind. The tactics and strategies used really don't matter as long as you achieve victory and don't out pace your replacement rate. History is full of generals who chose battle plans based on their egos and a desire to be remembered rather than what has the lowest casualty rate. Your job is to break, destabilize, and disable a given enemy faction, nation, government or military. It is not your job to worry about post war clean up or how the civilian population will recover or when the local economy will get back on its feet. If you are killed in battle, someone else will be promoted or otherwise put in charge of your troops.<br /> <br /> Horror isn't being a Twitch ethot and knowing that your simps are emptying their bank accounts to the detriment of their family's wellbeing but still accepting the money anyways. Horror isn't knowing bad people, nor is horror representing non-democratic governmental processes.<br /> <br /> Horror is the emotional reaction produced when you are not strong enough to deal with a situation or the requirements thereof. The General doesn't feel horror at the prospect of war, but the soldier in the trenches praying for the shelling to stop just for a little while feels endless horror.<br /> <br /> The problem with VtM as a game is that it wants to have personal horror as a component and as such its design practically forces conflict and infighting. Yet when you consider from an objective point of view how to fix the problems of the vampire setting and its society, the answers break the game design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:20:43-07:00","id":1515094,"title":"","content":"With that kind of behaviour, either every elder is smarter than Xanatos or they're all stupid fools rushing to hasten their demise. Or maybe there's no free will and methuselah are pulling literally every string. <br /> <br /> Yes, the prince probably never lacks legitimate sounding pretenses to break a promise, but does that mean he actually breaks his promises so frequently? Can the Prince bear such a reputation when the stability of his position is largely reliant on his relationship with the community? <br /> <br /> I'm all for vampires being a caricature of the rich, the powerful and the political but for that to work it needs to ring true. Once you get into the territory of farce you'll lose a lot of empathy from players, and your setting will begin to lack verisimilitude .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:44:01-07:00","id":1515112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515094#post1515094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that kind of behaviour, either every elder is smarter than Xanatos or they're all stupid fools rushing to hasten their demise. Or maybe there's no free will and methuselah are pulling literally every string.</div> </div> </div> </div>No clue. Probably all of them at once. I'm not sure the politics were usually intended to be that deep; <i>&quot;vampires just backstab and manipulate constantly because they're monsters and The Man<sup>TM</sup> and it's what they're conditioned/cursed to do, ok?.&quot; </i>Also something about a metaphor for rebellion, punk and selling out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the prince probably never lacks legitimate sounding pretenses to break a promise, but does that mean he actually breaks his promises so frequently? Can the Prince bear such a reputation when the stability of his position is largely reliant on his relationship with the community? </div> </div> </div>I guess VtM is just going with the assumption that all princes are just so powerful and scary nobody can question them, or something? Or paying their powerful friends very well.<br /> Personally, my ideal Camarilla Prince draws inspiration from a less benevolent Havelock Vetinari; a scarily competent bastard who nobody with a brain wants deposed because they keep the city functioning, and because your alternative is idiot tyrants who will inevitably drive the city into chaos and bloodshed getting rid of them. You can have those, and an unstable domain makes for a good story setting, but the guy's not going to last.<br /> (Or you can have figureheads and take a gamble about who's pulling the strings.)\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm all for vampires being a caricature of the rich, the powerful and the political but for that to work it needs to ring true. Once you get into the territory of farce you'll lose a lot of empathy from players, and your setting will begin to lack verisimilitude . </div> </div> </div>I don't even care about the caricatures, I just like my elders to be 3D, complicated individuals instead of dimensionless scary monsters to beat the pcs over the head with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-15-2023, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:45:59-07:00","id":1515113,"title":"","content":"And leaving my hyperbole about 99% of vampires being the most untrustworthy bastards on the planet aside; I compromise on it by making the vampire reputation for backstabbing villains be an in-universe thing that even vampires themselves kind of buy into, which is then reinforced by their instinctively cautious nature and the fact that politicking does actually happen with some frequency. Vampires aren't actively going to hurt each other or rock the boat for shits and giggles, but nor do they really care about each other, which makes you expendable to them and vice versa. Thus trust and deep emotional connections can be difficult to form and this has a knock on effect where vampires mostly have a purely &quot;professional&quot; relationship with each other. You don't want to go out of your way to help your fellow kindred outside of boons and emergencies, because they'd only take advantage of you, right? And if you have to sell somebody downriver to protect you and yours, you might feel bad, but you may well do it because you can't trust that they wouldn't do it to you if the situations were reversed.<br /> <br /> Also vampires <i>can</i> be friends with each other and be loyal without blood bonds, it's just hard to make those steps. I don't care how grimdark this setting wants itself to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T07:40:10-07:00","id":1515124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515113#post1515113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And leaving my hyperbole about 99% of vampires being the most untrustworthy bastards on the planet aside; I compromise on it by making the vampire reputation for backstabbing villains be an in-universe thing that even vampires themselves kind of buy into, which is then reinforced by their instinctively cautious nature and the fact that politicking does actually happen with some frequency..</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed<br /> Vampires are - at the end of the day, even the most monstorus Sabbat or Tzimisce or Vulcan-like True Brujah - only human after all<br /> With all its advantages and disadvantages<br /> Expect nothing from a vampire than you would't expect from a human basically<br /> Hmans are horrible... but in the meantime capable of amazing wonders and altruism<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515113#post1515113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also vampires <i>can</i> be friends with each other and be loyal without blood bonds, it's just hard to make those steps. I don't care how grimdark this setting wants itself to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cThere must be no regrets, no tears, no anxieties. Just go forward in all your beliefs, and prove to me that I am not mistaken in mine.\u201d<br /> - The First Doctor<br /> \u200b<br /> <i>\u201cThere\u2019s no point in being grown up if you can\u2019t be childish sometimes.\u201d</i><br /> - The Fourth Doctor<br /> <br /> \u201cSome people live more in 20 years than others do in 80. It\u2019s not the time that matters, it\u2019s the person.\u201d<br /> - The Tenth Doctor,<br /> <br /> \u201cThe way I see it, every life is a pile of good things and bad things. The good things don\u2019t always soften the bad things, but vice versa, the bad things don\u2019t always spoil the good things or make them unimportant.\u201d<br /> - The Eleventh Doctor<br /> <br /> \u201cNever be cruel. Never be cowardly. Hate is always foolish. Love is always wise. Always try to be nice, but never fail to be kind.\u201d<br /> - The Twelfth Doctor<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-15-2023, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T19:21:28-07:00","id":1515199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515068#post1515068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for me it's important to emphasize that the horror of VTM is less about the vampire's feelings or connection to god and more about the impact they have on the people around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is probably the case if you're not religious in the slightest, which many vampires are not.<br /> <br /> I've always had fun with the idea of a person being an atheist, getting embraced, and getting REALLY UNCOMFORTABLE with the fact that so much religion seems to be objectively true. And God and his Angels are assholes against EVEN BIGGER ASSHOLES. Which is essentially HELLBLAZER'S premise. John Constantine is a super hardcore punk atheist secular moralist stuck in a world with objectively real assholes in charge of reality.<br /> <br /> Which is interesting enough, HOW THE GAME IS SUPPOSED TO BE PLAYED in 1st Edition. Caine is the first vampire and he's cursed by God but you're not actually supposed to accept God is good and that it was justice. V:TM was made in the Bible Belt but the counterculture district of Atlanta. There's a strong religious undercurrent to the setting but the fundamental attitude is that Christianity may be literally correct in this world (or partially) but that doesn't mean it's not horribly unfair, authoritarian, and immoral to modern morals.<br /> <br /> If you want to understand the &quot;personal horror&quot; in terms that a non-religious player may enjoy, essentially it's part of the Gothic PUNK element. Which is to say, preferrably in a Monty Python-esque voice, &quot;You're just walking along minding your own business when a supernatural creature from a mythology you don't even believe in comes up to suck out your blood then force their own into you. Without even your consent! . Now you can't go out during the daytime, hunger for the blood of your neighbors, and are now are subject to murderous killing sprees every time you try and argue with the DMV or get cut off in traffic! Oh and a bunch of crazed Baptists and Catholics think you need to die for their religion! Which would be fine to say fuck off regarding but then the demons show up trying to recruit you too! Lousy sabbat!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no wrong way to play V:TM and go ahead play Angel or Hannibal King as a vampire superero or Blade. You can also play a Mob Hitman or government assassin turned vampire. The Signature Character for 1st Edition was basically a vigilante drug-fighting private detective. 3rd Edition abandoned all personal horror to play bisexual shadow ninjas and pop star Toreador Elders. Plus whatever the hell Theo Bell is when he's not being Blade.<br /> <br /> However, there's actually a lot of fun going with the basic, &quot;You are a perfectly normal twenty something to forty something person who has been turned into a vampire. Your entire understanding of how the world works from evolution to the government to the economy is turned upside down. How do you deal with that?&quot; It might not be 100% weepy horror but yes, in fact, it is fun to imagine, &quot;You can never see your family again and if they ever see you, the local vampire mob boss will kill you or them or both.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's fun to roleplay the sucky elements of vampirism without the stereotyped Louis, &quot;WHY AM I SO ALONE! *kills woman*.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2023, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:06:43-07:00","id":1515394,"title":"","content":"I never found it a depressing game line and took it that it would be somewhat dark and grim as we are playing vampires who need to feed on humanity to keep &quot;sane&quot; and that the horror being personal seemed to be perfect as the decades and later centuries would wear on you and you would be so different from your early nights or days as a mortal. I always found WarHammer 40K somewhat depressing or even Gears Of War with the near constant warfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T12:53:03-07:00","id":1515472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515199#post1515199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is probably the case if you're not religious in the slightest, which many vampires are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of vampires will acknowledge that while the unveiling of secret supernaturals is a strong indicator for Gods of some kind existing, proof that a specific religion is correct doesn't exist outside of non-canon gehenna supplements. I imagine the bulk of vampire opinions concerning Gods are something along the lines of deism: God exists but he isn't going to make his will known as he fully intends to leave us to our own devices. <br /> <br /> More to the point, to be a hermetic, you've got to acknowledge some kind of higher power IE all Tremere are religious, and while the lack of access to avatars is unfortunate, I don't think they see themselves as damned. If anything, they'll probably see the embrace brings the average mortal closer to God, as they transcend their mundane selves through the alchemy that is vitae and become more divine... of course the Tremere aren't going to preach this kind of view because it'll put a target on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T13:04:20-07:00","id":1515474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515199#post1515199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to understand the &quot;personal horror&quot; in terms that a non-religious player may enjoy, essentially it's part of the Gothic PUNK element. Which is to say, preferrably in a Monty Python-esque voice, &quot;You're just walking along minding your own business when a supernatural creature from a mythology you don't even believe in comes up to suck out your blood then force their own into you. Without even your consent! . Now you can't go out during the daytime, hunger for the blood of your neighbors, and are now are subject to murderous killing sprees every time you try and argue with the DMV or get cut off in traffic! Oh and a bunch of crazed Baptists and Catholics think you need to die for their religion! Which would be fine to say fuck off regarding but then the demons show up trying to recruit you too! Lousy sabbat!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or in other words, to be a conservative atheist in California working a night shift. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T19:09:03-07:00","id":1515711,"title":"","content":"The problem is that being a vampire doesn't prove there is a God or Christians are right, that's just vampire mythology an atheist can easily reject. <br /> I think the real personal horror lies in your relationship with humanity, and not with God","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T19:46:05-07:00","id":1515712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515711#post1515711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that being a vampire doesn't prove there is a God or Christians are right, that's just vampire mythology an atheist can easily reject.<br /> I think the real personal horror lies in your relationship with humanity, and not with God</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: I roleplayed a guy with that exact view and he had a mental breakdown when he was burned by a cross shoved on his face by a rare True Faith individual.<br /> <br /> Because ALL OF HIS ARGUMENTS fell apart when that happened and he had no idea how to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Notably, I roleplayed him immediately starting to suffer a downgrade of his humanity because his atheism was tied to his ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T11:05:53-07:00","id":1515763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515712#post1515712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: I roleplayed a guy with that exact view and he had a mental breakdown when he was burned by a cross shoved on his face by a rare True Faith individual.<br /> <br /> Because ALL OF HIS ARGUMENTS fell apart when that happened and he had no idea how to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Notably, I roleplayed him immediately starting to suffer a downgrade of his humanity because his atheism was tied to his ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you've got shit like <br /> Oh, the buddhist could also do that with sutras<br /> The indian dude called upon shiva to destroy me and it almost worked<br /> The vietnamese guy could whip out his folk-religion... symbol (sorry, I don't know), and half burned me to death. <br /> A normal guy can't operate the cross<br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly it's the dude with the cross, not the cross. Unless you're baali or something. <br /> Granted, you're unlikely to meet all these fellows in welshpool, wales, and that one guy is likely the only source of true faith you'll meet in your unlife, but still, I think you're just letting your strawman fall on purpose. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T17:55:22-07:00","id":1515810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515763#post1515763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then you've got shit like<br /> Oh, the buddhist could also do that with sutras<br /> The indian dude called upon shiva to destroy me and it almost worked<br /> The vietnamese guy could whip out his folk-religion... symbol (sorry, I don't know), and half burned me to death.<br /> A normal guy can't operate the cross<br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly it's the dude with the cross, not the cross. Unless you're baali or something.<br /> Granted, you're unlikely to meet all these fellows in welshpool, wales, and that one guy is likely the only source of true faith you'll meet in your unlife, but still, I think you're just letting your strawman fall on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. As a vampire you must accept magic. I can easily say that crosses have magical power and that's why they are a symbol for religious people. Nothing, absolutely nothing, can prove God exists if you are a staunch atheist or even a sceptic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T01:52:16-07:00","id":1515831,"title":"","content":"Another thing. <br /> If I were to make an atheist character who got embraced, I would probably work on the premise that some 'gods' probably existed, but they were ordinary supernatural entities given the aid of exaggeration and deception. IE Ymir, Yahweh or Ptah are just as valid as some vampire or spirit. Supernatural being just not-yet understood products of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T04:40:17-07:00","id":1515848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515763#post1515763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then you've got shit like<br /> Oh, the buddhist could also do that with sutras<br /> The indian dude called upon shiva to destroy me and it almost worked<br /> The vietnamese guy could whip out his folk-religion... symbol (sorry, I don't know), and half burned me to death.<br /> A normal guy can't operate the cross<br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly it's the dude with the cross, not the cross. Unless you're baali or something.<br /> Granted, you're unlikely to meet all these fellows in welshpool, wales, and that one guy is likely the only source of true faith you'll meet in your unlife, but still, I think you're just letting your strawman fall on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that really the INTERESTING way to do the story, though? Not much roleplaying to be had of, &quot;I rationalize away my preexisting viewpoint.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T05:30:08-07:00","id":1515851,"title":"","content":"I can imagine far less roleplaying with &quot;oh, this one event shattered one of my main defining characteristics, guess I'll experience &quot;character growth&quot; to become what the player considers normalcy. <br /> <br /> IRL, even when someone believes in something totally asinine they're very capable of using mental gymnastics and cognitive dissonance to slap away anything solid the opposition throws at them. Some folks will even double down on their beliefs and see opposing evidence as the devil's seeds. Now when you actually believe in something reasonable and have a well founded framework for it? <br /> <br /> If the event was so shocking, my response to such events would be to call in favours and research other accounts. New things need to be tested and understood properly after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T00:38:41-07:00","id":1515932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515848#post1515848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that really the INTERESTING way to do the story, though? Not much roleplaying to be had of, &quot;I rationalize away my preexisting viewpoint.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need God to have a good story either. An atheist character dealing with what it means to be an undead bloodsucking monster is as interesting as a &quot;converting to Christianity just because that's what most undead bloodsucking monsters around me believe&quot; one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T17:09:46-07:00","id":1515977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1515932#post1515932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need God to have a good story either. An atheist character dealing with what it means to be an undead bloodsucking monster is as interesting as a &quot;converting to Christianity just because that's what most undead bloodsucking monsters around me believe&quot; one</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to explain how that relates to my story because believing in God is a source of Cthulhu-ean SAN loss and horror in this example. It feels like secularism defending the disbelief in God as as anti-religious stance when &quot;God as a horrifying concept&quot; is a much bigger anti-religious stance.<br /> <br /> The question is not, &quot;atheist dealing with humanity&quot;, it's &quot;atheist trapped in a world that is fundamentally anti-humanist.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I'm always interested in exploring characters who have their beliefs radically challenged. I was always annoyed there were no player options for Infernalists or Nephandi characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T12:32:06-07:00","id":1524230,"title":"","content":"About atheist supernaturals, there's one thing we can know for sure: supernatural exists. In a world where some kind of wolf and man hybrid can punch concrete and suddenly a forest takes place and one other vampire can lock a ghost in a shell, deny some level of metaphysics is asinine. But there to go to the belief of gods (especially if you throw Setites in the mix) is a jump. Yeah, if older vampires are stronger, and older garou, why not older spirits and ghosts?<br /> And addressing the first question: no, I think Werewolf is the most depressing. They lost the war, Gaea is dead or in their final rales, Earth is doomed, and all you can do is playing the brave little soldier of an army that no longer exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","user":"MrDrika","date":". 10-18-2023, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T13:05:52-07:00","id":1524234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1514956#post1514956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have no idea...<br /> Actually, you do, but you know hat I ment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> Yeah, you are right<br /> Actually the Followers of Set should be like the Kuei-jin, but instead of the Thousand Hell of Yomi a potential Settie should be an escapee from Duat - the egyptian underworld basically Hell if you are not in a tiny portion of it aka. manage to gain acces to the Field of Reeds, where Osiris rules<br /> Serpents, the spawn of Apep, haunt the 12 caverns of Duat. They swim in the river and coil about the limbs of the unredeemed dead.<br /> The dead in Duat exist in darkness, blinded by it, relieved only by the nightly passage of the ship of Ra<br /> Along with their torments, the dead in Duat cannot breathe or speak. The &quot;Opening of the Mouth&quot; funerary ritual was meant to deliver the deceased from this unhappy condition.<br /> The dead in Duat rest in coffins, paralized, that open only when the sun-god Ra makes his nightly passage.<br /> Just to name a few<br /> Duat is... not the nicest place, it is literally Hell if you don't cheat your way thrugh it, filled with darkness, silence, sand, snakes, demons and quite nasty things even the Sun God have to fight and Mandjet, the <i>Boat</i> of <i>Millions of Years</i>\u200b needs quite a fighter crew to help him out (and the mightiest of them was <b>Sutekh...</b>)... even the domain of <b>Seker</b>, the original God of the Underworld whom Osiris basically dethroned, Imhet was seen as difficult, sandy terrain, not to mention according to the myth, Seker rules the Fifth Kingdom of Night, which is called &quot;Hidden&quot;, and is tasked with punishing the souls of evildoers by throwing them into a boiling lake. Only a tiny part is &quot;good&quot;, the Field of Reeds and the personal domain of Osiris... and there is the whole Scales and Feather of Ma'at against your heart, the 42 Judges who destroy you if you don't know their name, <b>Ammit</b> eagerly awaits to eat your soul if you fail the Scales<br /> And thats for the &quot;normal dead&quot;!<br /> However, when the damned died? Their flesh was torn away by demons and their mummy wrappings were removed so that their bodies were left to decompose. In the underworld that the blessed successfully navigate, their order of things is reversed, even to the extent that the damned have to walk upside down, eat their own excrement and drink their own urine. Their hands are tied behind their backs, often around stakes. Their heads and limbs are severed from their bodies and their flesh is cut off their bones. Their hearts are removed and their ba-souls are separated from their bodies, forever unable to return to them. They even loose their shadows, which were considered an important part of the ancient Egyptian being. They have no air and suffer from hunger and thirst, as they receive no funerary offerings. Worst of all, they are denied the reviving light of the sun god, who ignores them, even as they cry out load and wail when he passes them in the underworld at night.<br /> They are continuously punished by demons, who are the representatives of chaos. Indeed, the demons are often recruited from the ranks of the damned themselves, so that they torture and kill one another. They are subjected to knives and swords and to the fire of hell, often kindled by fire spitting snakes. These horrible punishments were carried out in the &quot;slaughtering place&quot; or &quot;place of destruction&quot;, and presided over by the fierce goddess <b>Sekhmet</b>, whose butchers hack their victims to pieces and burn them with inextinguishable fire, sometimes in deep pits or in cauldrons in which they are scorched, cooked and reduced to ashes. Demons feed on their entrails and drink their blood.<br /> Another location was the Lake of Fire, which was first mentioned in the Book of Two Ways in the Coffin Text (Spell 1054/1166) and illustrated in the Book of the Dead (Chapter 126). Like the &quot;outer darkness,&quot; it is a place of regeneration for the sun god and his blessed followers, to whom it provides nourishment and cool water, but a place of destruction for the damned. Birds even fly away from it when they experience the burning, bloody water and small the stench of putrefaction which rises from it. In chapter 126 of the Book of the Dead, its shores are guarded by four baboons who sit at the bow of the barque of Ra and who are usually connected to the sunrise. There, they act as judges of the divine tribunal in order to decide who might be granted access through &quot;the secret portals of the West&quot; and who will be delivered to the hellhound, who, according to another spell, is in charge of this place. That demon-god is the &quot;Swallower of Millions,&quot; responsible for devouring corpses, or their shadows, snatching hearts and inflicting injury without being seen (<b>Am-heh</b> was a dangerous god from the underworld whose name can be translated as 'devourer of millions', or eater of eternity. He lived in a lake of fire and was represented as a man with the head of a hunting dog.)<br /> Not to mention <b>Shezmu</b>\u200b, Demon-God of the Wine Press, Oils and Slaughterer of the Damned; after the deceased had died, it was he who caught the sinful ones for punishment. In Chapter 175 of The Book of the Dead Shesmu was known as &quot;Lord of the Blood&quot;. It was under the orders of Osiris, that he would chop up the evil ones, take their heads and toss them into a wine press, treating the heads as if they were grapes to create blood wine.<br /> \u200b<br /> The judgement of Ma'at and devoured by Ammit was actually an &quot;easy death&quot; compared others\u200b<br /> <br /> In this regard Sutekh came back from Hell, like the souls come back/escape from Yomi. Apophis (and even other gods of Duat) like the Yama Kings<br /> The Followers of Set calls themselves the Mesu Bedshet, the &quot;<i>Children</i> of <i>Rebellion</i>&quot; for a reason - with a twist, this makes the Children of Anubis, the Silent Striders technically the jailors of Duat/Hell the &quot;bad guys&quot; and enemies of the Followers of Set, just they forgot the reason\u200b<br /> <br /> Would make much more sense, considering the whole belief system of the Followers of Sutekh to be like the Kuei-jin rather like the get of Caine<br /> Or actually sell Sutekh as Caine... the murdering of thy brother is a tiny bit older story with Sutekh and Asar/Set and Osiris than Caine and Able...</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you... Just fix the Followers of Set, Mummy AND by contrast, perhaps KotE?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think I love you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T16:24:36-07:00","id":1524244,"title":"","content":"You know that becoming a vampire, werewolf or mage would be a most earth shattering thing if you think about it as it upends your deeply held belief of the world.<br /> <br /> That could be the best thing or worst thing to happen to you given what type of person you were depending on how you play the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T09:18:46-07:00","id":1524389,"title":"","content":"To answer the OP, yes, yes I do, of gamelines that I have played. It was really cool when I was an edgy 15 year old in the late 90's in my black leather trenchcoat. Now in my 30's and I game with my kids... No. I'm not letting them anywhere near this game, even though I enjoyed playing it all through high school and bit of college.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T02:01:45-07:00","id":1524516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1524389#post1524389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer the OP, yes, yes I do, of gamelines that I have played. It was really cool when I was an edgy 15 year old in the late 90's in my black leather trenchcoat. Now in my 30's and I game with my kids... No. I'm not letting them anywhere near this game, even though I enjoyed playing it all through high school and bit of college.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a teacher I think one of the most challenging dynamics is the fact both sides know we are appalling hypocrites. <br /> <br /> &quot;Well strictly speaking you're too young to be watching Alien....&quot;<br /> &quot;how old were you when you saw it miss?&quot;<br /> &quot;Errrrr&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T07:52:37-07:00","id":1524524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514933-does-anyone-else-find-vtm-to-be-the-most-depressing-gameline?p=1524516#post1524516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a teacher I think one of the most challenging dynamics is the fact both sides know we are appalling hypocrites.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well strictly speaking you're too young to be watching Alien....&quot;<br /> &quot;how old were you when you saw it miss?&quot;<br /> &quot;Errrrr&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of those things that, yes, I played it, but no, it wasn't good for my long term mental health. I frequently got quite depressed about my life and the world,VtM books and vtm rpg playing didn't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus",